{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLSIZ-20260904", "finding_id": "OLSIZ-004", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0034", "path": "content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/reduction.tex", "bytes": 5540, "sha256": "0d6d2e3280698668b837cef6dcf3134b86d2a4b48831ae516e6e33e42898c79a", "locator": "lines 47-69", "finding": "The definition calls f(Z) the sequence s_k although k is never bound or determined.", "controlling_evidence": "The component equation uniquely defines the characteristic sequence of Z, and the surjectivity argument later denotes an arbitrary output sequence by s.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": ["s_k", "s_k(n)"], "added": ["s", "s(n)"]}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/reduction.tex", "bytes": 5770, "sha256": "11ff639ead636b6bf93c911baac161f576aabc515613b2a043d27eddd769c38f", "adjacent_note_lines": [54], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 52, "line_end": 55, "sha256_utf8_lf": "562bc88fd813e30f6658ebdd53b6c011203f281cb6f5fbd85edf9ec9983c5c56"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the unbound characteristic-sequence name s_k by s throughout the definition."}, "audit_artifacts": {"findings_file": "FINDINGS.json", "findings_sha256": "9b6e836c8432eb75d331913983603796d6557da6ec3ad71b846b2a248374cd07", "review_file": "REVIEW.md", "review_sha256": "26913176baacbda5ae8a47bcc82ccf0366b0763313e6eeeb45df59e64249a1f9"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLSIZ-20260904", "finding_id": "OLSIZ-005", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0034", "path": "content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/reduction.tex", "bytes": 5540, "sha256": "0d6d2e3280698668b837cef6dcf3134b86d2a4b48831ae516e6e33e42898c79a", "locator": "lines 85-100", "finding": "The displayed h(n) is explicitly a finite string of n zeros, but h is declared to map into the set of infinite binary sequences.", "controlling_evidence": "Membership in Bin^omega requires an infinite binary sequence; appending an infinite tail, for example n zeros followed by ones forever, supplies the intended non-surjective example.", "mathematical_delta": {"display_tail_added": "an explicit infinite tail"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/reduction.tex", "bytes": 5770, "sha256": "11ff639ead636b6bf93c911baac161f576aabc515613b2a043d27eddd769c38f", "adjacent_note_lines": [102], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 100, "line_end": 103, "sha256_utf8_lf": "4eadfb0288fcd9110cf55f8d0d24a5f84f67250f90689774292b7c4529c065f7"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the finite zero string by n leading zeros followed by an infinite tail of ones."}, "audit_artifacts": {"findings_file": "FINDINGS.json", "findings_sha256": "9b6e836c8432eb75d331913983603796d6557da6ec3ad71b846b2a248374cd07", "review_file": "REVIEW.md", "review_sha256": "26913176baacbda5ae8a47bcc82ccf0366b0763313e6eeeb45df59e64249a1f9"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLSIZ-20260904", "finding_id": "OLSIZ-006", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0035", "path": "content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/equinumerous-sets.tex", "bytes": 4141, "sha256": "025a3fc368d6873825effcb07631913762edbf2d3f9a0711d57dcd9575361251", "locator": "lines 68-94", "finding": "Two conditional variants refer to g(x)=y before g is introduced, although the bijection in scope is f.", "controlling_evidence": "The proof has fixed f:A to B; g is introduced only later as an enumeration of A.", "mathematical_delta": {"occurrences": 2, "removed": "g(x)=y", "added": "f(x)=y"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/equinumerous-sets.tex", "bytes": 4352, "sha256": "d98271ec9b67b12c13f379e3c616b0fa86312a5ee043621000d0243f8541f66d", "adjacent_note_lines": [75, 92], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 73, "line_end": 76, "sha256_utf8_lf": "bb8de24cc024f141de2c7a697f9f77034bd9c418c61d03bd727e515b92a09ba4"}, {"line_start": 90, "line_end": 93, "sha256_utf8_lf": "93e718993f2933c12bf6bfadbc98a25e95c5a86f1bc156b5949acc6a07ca1007"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced both premature g(x)=y occurrences by f(x)=y."}, "audit_artifacts": {"findings_file": "FINDINGS.json", "findings_sha256": "9b6e836c8432eb75d331913983603796d6557da6ec3ad71b846b2a248374cd07", "review_file": "REVIEW.md", "review_sha256": "26913176baacbda5ae8a47bcc82ccf0366b0763313e6eeeb45df59e64249a1f9"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLSIZ-20260904", "finding_id": "OLSIZ-007", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0036", "path": "content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/comparing-size.tex", "bytes": 6677, "sha256": "075810b1cf1c8b54266518523d4665d3deae4a4937f4e19a66a09cc0e1aaebf7", "locator": "lines 74-90", "finding": "After choosing arbitrary x in A, the source says the conclusion holds for each x in overline(A).", "controlling_evidence": "To prove the diagonal set is outside the range, the argument needs g(x) different from overline(A) for every x in A; both preceding cases concern arbitrary x in A.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "x in overline(A)", "added": "x in A"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/comparing-size.tex", "bytes": 7183, "sha256": "68eef3a8a3adb8167bb1d919e8bc8bb7e2d6f109801f2fea8360a0674dc0bbab", "adjacent_note_lines": [93], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 91, "line_end": 94, "sha256_utf8_lf": "7d52945e87aa991c33396c26de723e3da919d5291d7242d07b2cc35f08c52cae"}], "applied_handling": "Quantified the diagonal conclusion over every x in A."}, "audit_artifacts": {"findings_file": "FINDINGS.json", "findings_sha256": "9b6e836c8432eb75d331913983603796d6557da6ec3ad71b846b2a248374cd07", "review_file": "REVIEW.md", "review_sha256": "26913176baacbda5ae8a47bcc82ccf0366b0763313e6eeeb45df59e64249a1f9"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLSIZ-20260904", "finding_id": "OLSIZ-008", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0039", "path": "content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/non-enumerability-alt.tex", "bytes": 6574, "sha256": "a075f6c63879101314fb20fa493acfb38d78ff24095bb55914f2af4527e1ad3e", "locator": "lines 61-75", "finding": "The prose calls s_n(m) the nth digit of the mth string, reversing the indices.", "controlling_evidence": "The next sentence and array place s_n(m) in row n and column m, so it is the mth digit of the nth string.", "mathematical_delta": null}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/non-enumerability-alt.tex", "bytes": 6958, "sha256": "5af7c817395540e2fc9137f8960a116d4822026b391797d65c80c974ef9967c1", "adjacent_note_lines": [68], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 66, "line_end": 69, "sha256_utf8_lf": "446a1a7812d704a002442d0ac1c2d87f0814e885b3b3aeac438322359388d211"}], "applied_handling": "Described s_n(m) as the mth digit of the nth string."}, "audit_artifacts": {"findings_file": "FINDINGS.json", "findings_sha256": "9b6e836c8432eb75d331913983603796d6557da6ec3ad71b846b2a248374cd07", "review_file": "REVIEW.md", "review_sha256": "26913176baacbda5ae8a47bcc82ccf0366b0763313e6eeeb45df59e64249a1f9"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
