{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLSIZ-20260904", "finding_id": "OLSIZ-010", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0040", "path": "content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/reduction-alt.tex", "bytes": 5500, "sha256": "f7717d8394048096cf7a65bc87a1a1ed15861cdfb8c7edb23429d5256d954d11", "locator": "lines 48-58", "finding": "The alternate proof again calls f(N) the string s_k although k is never bound or determined.", "controlling_evidence": "The component equation uniquely defines the characteristic sequence of N.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": ["s_k", "s_k(n)"], "added": ["s", "s(n)"]}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/reduction-alt.tex", "bytes": 5591, "sha256": "cc259462e3d7671ced74c079fffeb6172abf0c42a12658e819c40dcb53dab3bb", "adjacent_note_lines": [55], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 53, "line_end": 56, "sha256_utf8_lf": "8c22d46c4ecab141e5c15adafeee6c1326ecdbafd6255f77a821c6f77a37c87f"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the unbound characteristic-sequence name s_k by s throughout the definition."}, "audit_artifacts": {"findings_file": "FINDINGS.json", "findings_sha256": "9b6e836c8432eb75d331913983603796d6557da6ec3ad71b846b2a248374cd07", "review_file": "REVIEW.md", "review_sha256": "26913176baacbda5ae8a47bcc82ccf0366b0763313e6eeeb45df59e64249a1f9"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-001", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0058", "path": "content/propositional-logic/syntax-and-semantics/formulas.tex", "bytes": 7021, "sha256": "f05ab9c5e23b362dbee9f6063f096f52ebc9e7f97b29acc9c07f18788f1f8f48", "locator": "line 159", "finding": "The material-conditional abbreviation closes an outer parenthesis which it never opens.", "controlling_evidence": "The same file's binary-connective formation clauses enclose compound formulas in a matched outer parenthesis pair. The branch is intended to abbreviate the disjunction of not-A with B, and the unmatched delimiter is a presentation error rather than an alternate logical definition.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "$\\lnot !A \\lor !B)$", "added": "$(\\lnot !A \\lor !B)$"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/propositional-logic/syntax-and-semantics/formulas.tex", "bytes": 7311, "sha256": "4970549092af228a0eaab6c3b16092aaaa67f3de2c7e39c1ed6d8df1eb587c11", "adjacent_note_lines": [161], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 159, "line_end": 162, "sha256_utf8_lf": "f7ed89dfd121e5495df42c468e35d6b2ce9b48da4a47695759e16497706ab0b7"}], "applied_handling": "Restored the missing opening parenthesis in the material-conditional abbreviation."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL001_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "1d959ac9106318cc04e7fcace58d3c339aebf975eeee7d32419d198d4a04e16f"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-TABLEAU-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-002", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0067", "path": "content/first-order-logic/proof-systems/tableaux.tex", "bytes": 3914, "sha256": "8c9db50bcbc7a4aa757b8d57796b2e51df04b1cabb61f46756a79f72a1780b8f", "locator": "line 38", "finding": "The false-conjunction rule name receives the entire formula as its connective argument.", "controlling_evidence": "The immediately preceding true-conjunction rule is named with the conjunction connective alone. Every other false-conjunction rule name in the frozen corpus found by exact search uses \\TRule{\\False}{\\land}.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "\\TRule{\\False}{!A \\land !B}", "added": "\\TRule{\\False}{\\land}"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/proof-systems/tableaux.tex", "bytes": 4342, "sha256": "fee2c7294897cbcfaf087985b9c265c17872b02a6ff37f791347c3ee2f9d0b5d", "adjacent_note_lines": [41], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 39, "line_end": 43, "sha256_utf8_lf": "5521ad976641263f55519e3253032d75f58d669b7bc7c870fac94ffc16601088"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the full-formula rule-name argument by the conjunction connective."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_TABLEAU_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "f279183c761edada863c7ad07fba4a8f23d472852c5b9fe1c1a394696d491761"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-TABLEAU-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-003", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0067", "path": "content/first-order-logic/proof-systems/tableaux.tex", "bytes": 3914, "sha256": "8c9db50bcbc7a4aa757b8d57796b2e51df04b1cabb61f46756a79f72a1780b8f", "locator": "lines 57-58", "finding": "The example labels both children of a true conjunction as true-implication expansions.", "controlling_evidence": "The parent on line 2 of the displayed tableau is the signed formula true (A and B). Its two children are true A and true B, exactly the outputs of the true-conjunction rule described in the preceding paragraph.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "\\TRule{\\True}{\\lif}[2]", "added": "\\TRule{\\True}{\\land}[2]"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/proof-systems/tableaux.tex", "bytes": 4342, "sha256": "fee2c7294897cbcfaf087985b9c265c17872b02a6ff37f791347c3ee2f9d0b5d", "adjacent_note_lines": [68], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 66, "line_end": 70, "sha256_utf8_lf": "de8193217b2cbb4c1945395bf9ae9e3960653556f3a01b62f9809096c481b57b"}], "applied_handling": "Relabeled both true-conjunction expansions with the true-conjunction rule."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_TABLEAU_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "f279183c761edada863c7ad07fba4a8f23d472852c5b9fe1c1a394696d491761"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-SEQUENT-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-004", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0075", "path": "content/first-order-logic/sequent-calculus/proving-things.tex", "bytes": 12407, "sha256": "8c94fddc6d2f4c5faee64e84c1216e1c1ca096719b5528ea4faff753b906d303", "locator": "lines 177-180", "finding": "Two prose candidates in the De Morgan proof search omit the negation on the second disjunct.", "controlling_evidence": "The requested end-sequent on lines 155-156 has antecedent \\lnot !A \\lor \\lnot !B. The proof tree immediately following the prose uses \\lnot !A \\lor \\lnot !B in both candidate contexts. The next failed branch and the eventual correct derivation both require the negated second disjunct.", "mathematical_delta": {"occurrences": 2, "removed": "\\lnot !A \\lor !B", "added": "\\lnot !A \\lor \\lnot !B"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/sequent-calculus/proving-things.tex", "bytes": 12483, "sha256": "dfead5f68fbc8fecda36ba653b073be222ce632797de568169dedce9e33cdb73", "adjacent_note_lines": [179], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 177, "line_end": 181, "sha256_utf8_lf": "514831f81e251521e89dca87161a47c565cd733bb3d53ce51f196cb12b6a788e"}], "applied_handling": "Restored the missing negation on the second disjunct in both prose candidate sequents."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_SEQUENT_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "ed92bec06eb7ff03cb517505a4ede9f8c3cfb83a7676672d4bc68d23c411277f"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-SEQUENT-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-005", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0077", "path": "content/first-order-logic/sequent-calculus/proof-theoretic-notions.tex", "bytes": 5914, "sha256": "91c07ed071c2f9c18d3f10665b163b35dcc8636e7e0f27b4586aa9df63177a53", "locator": "lines 9-11", "finding": "The editorial note identifies the section as natural deduction although the file belongs to the sequent-calculus chapter.", "controlling_evidence": "The source path and both tag-controlled file identifiers place the section in the sequent-calculus chapter. The section defines provability using LK derivations of sequents and proves transitivity using Cut. The parallel natural-deduction chapter has its own separate proof-theoretic-notions file.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "for natural deduction", "added": "for the sequent calculus"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/sequent-calculus/proof-theoretic-notions.tex", "bytes": 6239, "sha256": "f49c8f53668c69af91098708b8c87a82224eb25eeea75812462e41c871a931d0", "adjacent_note_lines": [11], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 9, "line_end": 13, "sha256_utf8_lf": "289bbd6f33621d0f83b0d2e4193cb430f5411bb141a6ed65fed92b1063aaa63f"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the incorrect natural-deduction chapter name by sequent calculus in the editorial note."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_SEQUENT_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "ed92bec06eb7ff03cb517505a4ede9f8c3cfb83a7676672d4bc68d23c411277f"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-SOUNDNESS-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-006", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0081", "path": "content/first-order-logic/sequent-calculus/soundness.tex", "bytes": 17663, "sha256": "4de487cafc9d685844abb2c0b29c7b51debeb30a9b1129c7a2fa8c13ae48b151", "locator": "lines 154-159", "finding": "The left-conjunction case concludes that its premise is valid instead of the displayed conclusion.", "controlling_evidence": "The case sets \\Theta to !A \\land !B, \\Gamma and \\Xi to \\Delta. The immediately preceding sentence proves that the arbitrary structure or valuation satisfies !A \\land !B, \\Gamma \\Sequent \\Delta. The induction hypothesis already supplied validity of the premise !A, \\Gamma \\Sequent \\Delta; the purpose of the case is to prove validity of its conclusion.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "$\\Gamma \\Sequent \\Delta$", "added": "$!A \\land !B, \\Gamma \\Sequent \\Delta$"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/sequent-calculus/soundness.tex", "bytes": 18606, "sha256": "771a51a29c7c8e79971b8cc699bda691fb4b64543e1c9c9d64b611e0a7f7da4a", "adjacent_note_lines": [167], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 165, "line_end": 169, "sha256_utf8_lf": "8366d5b7049a5b7a1117b9bc13499466160896872dde2670d2f25a040a0b63b9"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the already-assumed premise by the displayed left-conjunction conclusion in the final validity sentence."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_SOUNDNESS_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "ef8c8bfae0c8f27e2c1d9f7b00651fa6eb5e0bd1d7506a5868efd22169c13964"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-SOUNDNESS-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-007", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0081", "path": "content/first-order-logic/sequent-calculus/soundness.tex", "bytes": 17663, "sha256": "4de487cafc9d685844abb2c0b29c7b51debeb30a9b1129c7a2fa8c13ae48b151", "locator": "lines 282-289", "finding": "The Cut case prints set difference where its displayed right premise requires a sequent.", "controlling_evidence": "The displayed right premise is !A, \\Pi \\Sequent \\Lambda. In case (b), !A is true, so satisfaction of that premise requires exactly the semantic condition expressed by \\Pi \\Sequent \\Lambda. The Cut conclusion combines \\Gamma, \\Pi on the left and \\Delta, \\Lambda on the right; set difference has no role in this argument.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "$\\Pi \\setminus \\Lambda$", "added": "$\\Pi \\Sequent \\Lambda$"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/sequent-calculus/soundness.tex", "bytes": 18606, "sha256": "771a51a29c7c8e79971b8cc699bda691fb4b64543e1c9c9d64b611e0a7f7da4a", "adjacent_note_lines": [314], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 312, "line_end": 316, "sha256_utf8_lf": "7ea38b04189117831b23d3f1a40532c505302c7ed3d08224bc9f5e7ca245f937"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced set difference by the right-premise sequent required in the Cut validity case."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_SOUNDNESS_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "ef8c8bfae0c8f27e2c1d9f7b00651fa6eb5e0bd1d7506a5868efd22169c13964"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-NATURAL-DEDUCTION-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-008", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0085", "path": "content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/rules-and-proofs.tex", "bytes": 2061, "sha256": "e6e8bed6816bd64ac24342fd4d591ca0e7c1ddf82fc056b452aa87c45d810506", "locator": "lines 31-36", "finding": "The node-type noun switches from sentences to sequents inside the natural-deduction derivation definition.", "controlling_evidence": "Lines 31-32 expressly define natural-deduction derivations as trees of sentences whose topmost sentences are assumptions. Lines 34-36 call the upper and lower nodes of each inference sentences and identify them as premises and conclusion. No sequent is introduced as a node type anywhere in this natural-deduction definition.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "one, two, or three other sequents", "added": "one, two, or three other sentences"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/rules-and-proofs.tex", "bytes": 2229, "sha256": "9737415434b500f77edaa603bf4d39e5b5349fc469c024d4b9149c4924a27dc9", "adjacent_note_lines": [34], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 32, "line_end": 36, "sha256_utf8_lf": "66d255a589035b85380045c21a5c9de2c2d2e15b841ada15635c91e399140688"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the stray sequent node noun with sentence in the natural-deduction derivation description."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_NATURAL_DEDUCTION_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "5f8b01c98e161803045c7c195a4b86f33f62c5a45be88c9252d140edc52ffe86"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-NATURAL-DEDUCTION-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-009", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0087", "path": "content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/quantifier-rules.tex", "bytes": 4001, "sha256": "eb6d95a24fce278404457d9169c033645853aab7e1c22dd4ca1fec9595068313", "locator": "lines 58-61", "finding": "The blanket exclusion from the premises contradicts both displayed rules and the precise side conditions immediately above.", "controlling_evidence": "The displayed universal-introduction rule necessarily has premise A(a); its detailed condition excludes a from the universal conclusion and undischarged assumptions, not from that premise. The displayed existential-elimination subderivation necessarily begins with the discharged assumption A(a); lines 52-56 expressly exempt those assumptions while excluding a from the existential premise, conclusion and other undischarged assumptions. The two rules therefore require distinct occurrence checks and cannot be summarized as excluding the eigenvariable from every premise.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "the blanket phrase 'neither occur in the premises'", "added": "the rule-specific conclusion, existential-premise and undischarged-assumption restrictions stated immediately above"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/quantifier-rules.tex", "bytes": 4353, "sha256": "979a2225226b518223cce43dcb9e14958977d453ebb792a5b64a63f74cfcdca5", "adjacent_note_lines": [62], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 60, "line_end": 64, "sha256_utf8_lf": "8160032f1fa597ba8ef9b766247fdaf4bcf79dfc5bfda9c86faaa06e4ee100d2"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the blanket no-premise-occurrence summary with the rule-specific eigenvariable restrictions stated immediately above."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_NATURAL_DEDUCTION_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "5f8b01c98e161803045c7c195a4b86f33f62c5a45be88c9252d140edc52ffe86"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-NATURAL-DEDUCTION-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-010", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0089", "path": "content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/proving-things.tex", "bytes": 11062, "sha256": "d39069643439c576cb5813ef635725ac09ef83257571e380b92dfa223a801ecc", "locator": "lines 129-136", "finding": "The completed proof tree labels a negation-elimination inference as falsehood introduction.", "controlling_evidence": "Lines 116-126 describe the same two premises and label the corresponding partial-tree inference \\Elim{\\lnot}. The propositional rule definition derives falsum from \\lnot !A and !A under the label \\Elim{\\lnot}. Lines 127-128 then invoke \\FalseInt only for the separate step from falsum to !B.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "\\RightLabel{\\Intro{\\lfalse}}", "added": "\\RightLabel{\\Elim{\\lnot}}"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/proving-things.tex", "bytes": 11656, "sha256": "ad562a558dae1511d0a0294a227c4dcef8998f0bbd3f62286a1605a30ebf757f", "adjacent_note_lines": [151], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 149, "line_end": 153, "sha256_utf8_lf": "7519cb2fd16e7a4874dc53865363cf9e707fcd6db7fb40c97c6f19937f6647cc"}], "applied_handling": "Relabeled the inference from a negation and its positive sentence to falsum as negation elimination."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_NATURAL_DEDUCTION_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "5f8b01c98e161803045c7c195a4b86f33f62c5a45be88c9252d140edc52ffe86"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-NATURAL-DEDUCTION-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-011", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0089", "path": "content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/proving-things.tex", "bytes": 11062, "sha256": "d39069643439c576cb5813ef635725ac09ef83257571e380b92dfa223a801ecc", "locator": "lines 116-119", "finding": "The prose gives the wrong side for the second branch.", "controlling_evidence": "In the displayed tree immediately above, the \\lnot !A and !A subderivation is the middle branch and the !B with !A subderivation is the rightmost branch. Line 149 begins the discussion of that same subderivation with 'the rightmost branch.' The leftmost branch is occupied by the disjunction assumption used as the major premise of disjunction elimination.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "on the left", "added": "on the right"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/proving-things.tex", "bytes": 11656, "sha256": "ad562a558dae1511d0a0294a227c4dcef8998f0bbd3f62286a1605a30ebf757f", "adjacent_note_lines": [119], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 117, "line_end": 121, "sha256_utf8_lf": "3059fdd2eef9716374bc517c8da1f8e84d293268f330e803d6bd370dbd128358"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the incorrect left-branch direction with the rightmost branch shown by the proof tree and next paragraph."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_NATURAL_DEDUCTION_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "5f8b01c98e161803045c7c195a4b86f33f62c5a45be88c9252d140edc52ffe86"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098fe", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLPL-NATURAL-DEDUCTION-20260905", "finding_id": "OLPL-012", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0090", "path": "content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/proving-things-quant.tex", "bytes": 9548, "sha256": "962c30713b222744c165ce87f7cb8ab11d18d0e805d8d386900bfe8e8104f63f", "locator": "lines 35-40", "finding": "The prose cites the wrong existential formula while setting up existential elimination.", "controlling_evidence": "The requested implication has antecedent \\lexists[x][\\lnot !A(x)]. Every partial and completed proof tree uses \\lexists[x][\\lnot !A(x)] as the major premise of existential elimination. Restoring the negation does not change the set of constants in the formula, so the freshness conclusion remains the same.", "mathematical_delta": {"removed": "$\\lexists[x][!A(x)]$", "added": "$\\lexists[x][\\lnot !A(x)]$"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/first-order-logic/natural-deduction/proving-things-quant.tex", "bytes": 9896, "sha256": "8ff08199096e9191e399be37aedb60a24f42156c7ab27402cdedf59b958f7786", "adjacent_note_lines": [40], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 38, "line_end": 42, "sha256_utf8_lf": "5a905786d8efd8484fc58f75768996672935a42bfaf5736f5e1ea662cc986564"}], "applied_handling": "Restored the negation in the existential premise named by the eigenvariable discussion and every adjacent proof tree."}, "audit_artifacts": {"review_file": "OLPL_NATURAL_DEDUCTION_SOURCE_AUDIT.json", "review_sha256": "5f8b01c98e161803045c7c195a4b86f33f62c5a45be88c9252d140edc52ffe86"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "7790323d5695b5174a0f7db9581e383913396ede609245b76955e884e304bfce", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "120360354305a4ab517c93ef024aa4adff9c14e171f1d6dc749cb3d5066098